# Contact addresses shown on /contact. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the
# real values for local development. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is the
# committed template (no real values).
#
# IMPORTANT: this is a STATIC site. These addresses render into the published
# HTML and are visible to anyone viewing the page — the PUBLIC_ prefix makes
# that explicit. Env here keeps the values out of the git REPO (and out of code
# search), not out of the browser. Don't put anything truly secret here.
#
# In CI/production these come from a GitHub Actions secret (see
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml and the README's deploy section).

# General contact — the public "tell me about your bookstore" inbox.
PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=contact@example.com

# Tech support / problems with the site.
PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
